    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονεμ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>disposed to distribute</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
				ἀ. [ἦθος</span>] disposition <i>to give every one his
				due,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				1.16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκάστῳ τῶν πρὸς ἀξίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					19.384
				</span></i>
			; <i>distributive,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Asp.
			</span></i><i>in</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>EN</u>
				158.22
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					7.126
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονεμετ-</span> is a
		f.l.)</div>
